      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(hooks): report agent startup admission failures",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`/hooks/agent` could return HTTP success as soon as an isolated agent run was queued, even if the run failed before reaching runner-entry/session admission. For Symphony Kanban this made a hook dispatch look durable while the worker had actually hit a lifecycle/startup failure such as:\n\n`Session \"agent:herbert-karajan:hook:symphony-kanban\" changed while starting work. Retry.`\n\nThat left the board with an accepted dispatch but no reliable worker closeout path.\n\nThis PR changes agent hook dispatch so startup/admission failures surface through the HTTP response before the idempotency key is cached:\n\n- waits for `onExecutionStarted` before returning `{ ok: true, runId }`\n- returns `409` for changed/deleted/archived session startup failures\n- returns `503` if runner entry does not start before the admission timeout\n- returns `502` for other pre-start failures\n- keeps post-start failures on the existing async/log/system-event path\n- preserves hook session-key policy and `deliver:false` behavior\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/test-projects.mjs src/gateway/hooks.test.ts src/gateway/hooks-mapping.test.ts src/gateway/server.hooks.test.ts src/gateway/server-http.hooks-request-timeout.test.ts src/gateway/server/hooks.agent-trust.test.ts`\n  - passed: 16 files / 314 tests\n- `node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p tsconfig.core.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/core.tsbuildinfo`\n  - passed\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`\n  - passed\n\n## Operational Boundary\n\nThis is source-only. It does not restart or modify any live gateway config by itself. Runtime activation still requires the normal deployment path and an approved gateway refresh.\n\n## Related Tracking\n\n- KAN-278: implementation card for the hook-session routing/admission fix.\n- KAN-223: live worker smoke target after merge/deploy/gateway refresh.\n- KAN-267: superseded duplicate investigation card.\n",
